{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix pushed as Gerrit change 2631 (commit 957aff4c0eba), NOT yet closed.\n\nRED first, on origin/main tip cfff861c061c in a clean worktree:\n  `pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py::test_a_marker_in_a_new_gate_scripts_head_admits_it`\n  -> ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'scripts._mechanism_delta'\nThe same node under `python -m pytest` passed, confirming the reported mechanism\n(cwd on sys.path under -m, absent under the bare console script).\n\nFix, scoped to tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py only:\nthe module now installs its own sys.path entry at import time, derived from __file__,\nand imports `_mechanism_delta.markers` by bare name - the same pattern\nscripts/check_mechanism_delta.py already uses to reach that subpackage.\nscripts/_mechanism_delta/__init__.py needed no change.\n\nScope decision (the broader alternative was considered and rejected):\na repo-root conftest.py or a pythonpath setting would fix this and every future case,\nbut the repo root being OFF sys.path is a load-bearing invariant here - it is what\ntests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py (bug a371) enforces. Putting the root on the\npath would make `tests.`-rooted imports resolve under the bare console script and reduce\nthat standing guard to a no-op. An AST sweep also found exactly ONE package-form\n`scripts.` import in the whole repository - the one removed here - so the narrow fix is\nalso the complete one. file_impact unchanged.\n\nAC3 guard: test_the_reported_selection_passes_standalone spawns the BARE pytest console\nscript from a cwd outside the repository and asserts the reported node passes. Proven to\nbe a real oracle, not a change detector: with the insert removed it fails even under\n`python -m pytest`, the invocation that originally masked the defect.\n\nVerification: node RED->GREEN under the bare script; `python -m pytest` still green;\nwhole module 32 passed under BOTH invocation styles; both sibling import-convention\nguards still green; make lint and make typecheck exit 0 with no ratchet baseline edits\nand no new mechanism."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788552786318141001,"uuid":"8b70b5dd-2d6e-43ab-9d58-16b35d055fd6"}